      ⍝ huge left argument regression ----------------------------------
      ⍝ A f/B computed n_wise as a plain (32-bit) int from A (a full 64-
      ⍝ bit APL_Integer), so a huge A truncated down to whatever 32 bits
      ⍝ it happened to land on -- occasionally negative, which then
      ⍝ slipped past the "n_wise > B's axis length" DOMAIN ERROR check
      ⍝ (negative is never > a small positive bound), while the actual
      ⍝ reduction loop further down still used the untruncated, huge,
      ⍝ unchecked A to compute an out-of-bounds ravel offset into B --
      ⍝ a real SEGV. Any of these hanging or crashing (instead of
      ⍝ DOMAIN ERROR) is a regression; the exact numbers are otherwise
      ⍝ arbitrary.

      3550579489682168305 +/ 1 2 3 4 5
DOMAIN ERROR+
      3550579489682168305+/1 2 3 4 5
      ^                  ^

      →

